  "taskDemand": "Extend the submitted AbilityStage with an owned ApplicationContext environment subscription lifecycle. After a successful onCreate there must be exactly one active application environment callback; repeated creates may retain or replace that owned callback but must not accumulate subscriptions. A registration failure must allow retry on the next create. Callback ID 0 is valid. onDestroy must unregister only the owned callback through ApplicationContext.off('environment', callbackId), release local ownership, and allow a fresh subsequent create. Destroy before creation and repeated destroy must not attempt invalid cancellation. Active configuration and memory callbacks must preserve the original logging of language/colorMode and memory level, with no callback delivery after destruction. Preserve the original imports, default export and guide marker pair. This is a new frozen task extension, not a claim of an upstream defect; assessment is only controlled ApplicationContext host seams, not platform lifecycle dispatch, SDK errors, module.srcEntry, ArkTS build or full candidate qualification.",
  "workerPath": "scripts/environment-lifecycle-worker.cjs",
  "compilerSha256": "3ae902c92cc44dace175c0e69e13a4b0899f6983c6121d76b9ab8dd5795e7675",
